{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PUU1BhnSeWMyS5Szinywv5","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, the broker/executor config that controls the number of threads used for offloading assignment computation in KIP-1263 (about reducing group coordinator load by batching assignment recalculations) is:\\\\n\\\\n**`group.coordinator.background.threads`**\\\\n\\\\nThis configuration controls the number of threads in the group coordinator's CoordinatorExecutor thread pool, which is used for processing background/asynchronous tasks such as computing assignments.\\\\n\\\\n**Sources:**\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/23/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21555-opened-92a8cbec.md` — PR #21555 that introduces this config, titled \\\\\\\"KAFKA-20210: Add group.coordinator.background.threads config\\\\\\\"\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/24/github-api-apache-kafka-review-comment-PRRC_kwDOACG9q86plOY3-bf4ab17a.md` — Review comment describing the config's purpose for computing assignments\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/03/01/mail-4f7fd3d7ae5bfb5b7fd2a661-eccd0f4d.md` — Mailing list discussion mentioning the config was renamed from `group.coordinator.executor.threads` to `group.coordinator.background.threads`\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"events/2026/03/12/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21720-opened-3cd35ce6.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/03/12/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21721-opened-d22b5c67.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/03/12/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21722-opened-b8712ab2.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/03/06/mail-90579402181d02d6437be19b-c254ac5c.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/03/07/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21662-opened-d17e834a.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/24/github-api-apache-kafka-review-comment-PRRC_kwDOACG9q86plOY3-bf4ab17a.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/23/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21555-opened-92a8cbec.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/03/03/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21555-merged-b02027d3.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/03/01/m